export const title = "Email Alert";
export const html = "<h1>Email Alert</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<p>When an event occurs, you can send the event snapshot and event metadata by email.</p>\n\n<h2>Configuring an Email Action Using an SMTP Server</h2>\n<p>An email action using an SMTP server can be added from the action settings screen.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>Email(SMTP)</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Setting the action type to <strong>Email(SMTP)</strong> reveals the related settings below it.</p>\n\n<p>If you set up your own SMTP server and authentication information, you can build an email-sending action using that SMTP server.</p>\n<p>Click the <span class=\"btn small primary\">New</span> tab to register a new SMTP server configuration. Once an SMTP server configuration is registered, it can be referenced from any event action.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\" style=\"max-width:480px;margin:0 auto;\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">SMTP Server</div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:150px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n      <span>Name</span><input value=\"My SMTP\" disabled>\n      <span>Provider</span><select disabled><option>Hotmail</option></select>\n      <span>SMTP Server</span><span><input value=\"smtp-mail.outlook.com\" disabled style=\"width:70%;display:inline-block;\"> <input value=\"587\" disabled style=\"width:25%;display:inline-block;\"></span>\n      <span>Encryption</span><select disabled><option>TLS</option></select>\n      <span>Validate Server Certificate</span><select disabled><option>On</option></select>\n      <span>From email</span><input disabled>\n      <span>SMTP Authentication</span><input type=\"checkbox\" checked disabled style=\"width:auto;\">\n      <span>Username</span><input value=\"MY_USERNAME\" disabled>\n      <span>Password</span><input value=\"&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;&bull;\" disabled>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"modal-foot\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Apply</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>SMTP server configuration</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Name</strong> &ndash; a name to identify this SMTP server in the list.</li>\n<li><strong>Provider</strong> &ndash; a template with preset information from companies that offer common public SMTP servers. If you've set up your own SMTP server, choose <strong>Custom</strong> and enter each field yourself.</li>\n<li><strong>SMTP Server</strong> &ndash; enter the SMTP server's address and port.</li>\n<li><strong>Encryption</strong> &ndash; choose the encryption method used by the server, such as SSL/TLS.</li>\n<li><strong>Validate Server Certificate</strong> &ndash; when set to ON, the certificate the server presents is verified against a certificate authority. If the certificate isn't verified by a certificate authority, email won't be sent.</li>\n<li><strong>From email</strong> &ndash; if required by the SMTP server, enter the sender's email address.</li>\n<li><strong>Authentication</strong> &ndash; enter the SMTP server's authentication information.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>Once an SMTP server is added, it appears in the SMTP server list. Select an item to configure an email-sending action.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:12.5px;margin-bottom:10px;\">SMTP Server &nbsp; <span class=\"btn small primary\">New</span></div>\n  <div style=\"border:1px solid var(--blue); background:var(--blue-light); border-radius:6px; padding:10px 12px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--blue);\">&#9679; My SMTP Server</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:4px;\">SMTP Server &nbsp; smtp-mail.outlook.com : 587<br>Username &nbsp; MY_USERNAME</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>SMTP server list</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Snapshots and video clips can be attached to email actions &ndash; see the <a href=\"/video-clip-snapshot\">Video Clip / Snapshot</a> guide for the steps.</p>";
